                                                "sense_id": "1ab77491-e987-3c8a-8f90-872aab05ca41",
                                                "text": "I was aware that some one, apparently at a vast distance, was calling me by my Christian name. [...] In the short space it took to cover the road between the path from Hamilton's shop and the first plank of the Combermere Bridge I had thought over half-a-dozen people who might have committed such a solecism, and had eventually decided that it must have been some singing in my ears."
                                            }
